; CURRENT-AXIS T-NUT FIELD GRID: 60 holes, no perimeter ring or outline.
; MACHINE XY centers: X47.5..547.5 and Y50..950, 100 mm pitch.
; These translate the old grid after the short-origin shifts and long-axis reversal.
; Requires current XY work offset 0,0; set a NEW tool Z0 for the 1/8-inch cutter.
; Tool: 3.175 mm single-flute upcut, at least 13 mm usable cutting length required.
; Finished bores: nominal diameter 7.000 mm, work Z-13.000 mm.
; Helix pitch 0.5 mm/rev at F600; outer finishing circles F900; XY travel F6000.
; Inner 1 mm orbit clears the center; outer 1.9125 mm orbit cuts the 7 mm wall.
; Each 0.5 mm layer is cleared before descending. Chip-clear retract every 2 mm.
; A flat outer circle at each layer plus the inner endpoint clears the whole floor.
; Tool-center retracts to Z10 between holes. Router power is manual.
; Pause at first center BEFORE cutting, and after first finished hole for a fit check.
; No automatic home, G92, tool offset reset, perimeter cut, or automatic motor disable.
G21
G90
G17
M220 S100
LED_ON
START_JOB
G1 Z10.0000 F600
G1 X47.5000 Y50.0000 F6000
M400
RESPOND MSG="First center X47.5 Y50. Check table alignment, NEW cutter surface Z0, and at least 13 mm cutting-flute length. Turn router ON manually and Resume only when ready."
PAUSE
; Hole 1/60: center X47.5000 Y50.0000, diameter 7, depth 13
